## Facts
Supervisor's serialized gate (`/tmp/claude-1000/-home-hep7-project-zlink/be443aad-d720-4c23-9860-099f913fdfd4/scratchpad/gate7-java-samples.log:181-190`):
Bingo `session-b.log` and `play-b.log` show `READY=1 TERMINATION=1 STOPPED_NONE=0 FORCE_STOPPED=1`, `outcome=FORCE_STOPPED reason=TEARDOWN_FAILED`;
`runner-common.sh:157-161` prints "Framework lifecycle evidence is incomplete" but the aggregate still exited 0. The role logs were overwritten by later
samples — rerun Bingo first (`bash samples/java/Bingo/run_sample.sh` or the aggregate's per-sample entry) and keep the logs. dotnet and node treat any
role not ending `Stopped/None` as a sample failure (dotnet runners `8e76335988`, node `8159b15752`).

## Fix (single owner each; rule count before/after)
1. Bingo teardown: find which Spot/Instance cleanup callback throws (or which owned resource fails to release) in session-b/play-b at HostShutdown —
   framework `ZLinkFrameworkRuntime.closeAllAsync()` / `ZLinkSpotLifecycle` / `ZLinkInstanceSpotActivation.close(HOST_SHUTDOWN)` or the sample's
   own `onClosing`. Root-cause it (compare with the dotnet fixes B1–B3 in `fix-dotnet-zoneworld-g4-and-teardown-outcomes-summary.md`: shutdown
   starting relocations, discovery/runtime stop order, authority Delete + shared capacity counter CAS contention — java's repository batches capacity
   on Delete the same way, so the same contention is a prime suspect). Fix at the owner, regression test at that layer.
2. Runner: "lifecycle evidence incomplete" must fail the sample and the aggregate (one rule: every host role ends `Stopped/None`, the `client` CLI and
   an intentional crash role excepted as in dotnet/node). No new reporting path — make the existing evidence check the failure owner.
3. ZoneWorld sample `samples/java/ZoneWorld/Server/.../zone/actors/PlayerActor.java:222`: only `UNAVAILABLE` maps to the client-visible "Unavailable";
   `DEADLINE_EXCEEDED`/`SHUTTING_DOWN` keep their own kinds (compare the node/dotnet ZoneWorld servers and the sample spec; the client assertion
   stays). Then run ZoneWorld and report honestly whether G4 still passes — if G4 now fails with DeadlineExceeded, that is the java durable sender
   lacking D-093 rule 1 (see `decisions.ko.md` D-093): implement rule 1 in `ZLinkJavaDurableRequest`/mesh node the same way (lifecycle terminal =
   Location/auto-connect owner removed the target's connection intent and no admitted peer remains → `Unavailable`; physical disconnect alone keeps
   replaying), with a unit regression, and re-run ZoneWorld.

